<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <div class="meta">CUDD Energy Services — TMV Preventive Maintenance SMS Program · Effective date: July 23, 2026</div>

  <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
  <p>This SMS program is operated by CUDD Energy Services ("we," "us") to send maintenance dispatch and work-order notifications to field technicians and contracted service personnel through the TMV Preventive Maintenance web application (<code>https://tmvapp.local-journal.com</code>).</p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only the information needed to deliver work-related SMS messages:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mobile phone number</strong> — provided by the technician in their app profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Name and role</strong> — to route the correct assignments.</li>
    <li><strong>Message content</strong> — dispatch tickets, unit/vessel identifiers (e.g., TMV-4471), van type, assigned functions, and the work-order link. This content is operational and contains no sensitive financial or health information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send maintenance dispatch, assignment, and work-order completion notifications.</li>
    <li>To confirm receipt and log completion of assigned functions in the PM app.</li>
    <li>We do <strong>not</strong> sell, rent, or share phone numbers or message content with third parties for marketing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Message Frequency &amp; Rates</h2>
  <p>Message frequency varies with assigned work — typically 1–10 messages per day per technician. Standard message and data rates may apply under your mobile carrier plan.</p>

  <h2>5. Your Choices &amp; Opt-Out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reply <code>STOP</code> to any message to opt out of SMS alerts. You will receive a confirmation and no further messages.</li>
    <li>Reply <code>HELP</code> for assistance, or email the program administrator.</li>
    <li>You may also disable SMS in your TMV PM app profile at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Data Retention &amp; Security</h2>
  <p>Phone numbers and message logs are stored on access-controlled servers and retained only as long as the technician relationship is active, after which they are removed. We use TLS in transit and restricted access controls at rest.</p>

  <h2>7. Contact</h2>
  <p>For privacy questions or to request deletion of your mobile number, contact the PM app administrator via the dispatcher console or reply <code>HELP</code> to a message.</p>

  <div class="footer">This policy satisfies carrier 10DLC consent and privacy disclosures for A2P messaging.</div>
